Oct 1, 2026 14:00 UTC","date":"Wed Sep 16 2026 11:00:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","hasContent":true,"body":"Raj moved Aozora logo review (internal) to Thu Oct 1, 2026, 14:00-15:00 UTC.\r\n"},"toolCallId":"call-cc7119ed-256e-46bd-bfd8-4a75bdf31f51","toolName":"getEmail","args":{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM5Nl0"}},"updatedAt":1793974987810},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1793974987812,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"The Northbeam Air flight is 9 Nov 2026 — three days from now (turn date Nov 6). That''s clearly the most urgent. Departure 18:30 from Frankfurt to Tokyo Haneda, arriving 14:15 next day, seat 14C unchanged.\n\nSo the answer: the Northbeam Air schedule change. It''s the only item with a live deadline — flight in 3 days.\n\nNote: the email says \"now departs at 18:30\" — implying a change from an earlier time, but the original time isn''t stated. So I can''t say how much it moved. Worth flagging: check the original booking time / whether the connection still works.\n\nAlso note the Linkroom renewal already happened Oct 3 — no action needed, it said so.\n\nI should be concise. Also could offer to check calendar for the flight / add a reminder. Keep it short.\n\nShould I mention that the flight is in 3 days and the email is 7 weeks old — meaning it may have been missed. Yes.\n\nLet me answer.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The Northbeam Air flight is 9 Nov 2026 — three days from now (turn date Nov 6). That''s clearly the most urgent. Departure 18:30 from Frankfurt to Tokyo Haneda, arriving 14:15 next day, seat 14C unchanged.\n\nSo the answer: the Northbeam Air schedule change. It''s the only item with a live deadline — flight in 3 days.\n\nNote: the email says \"now departs at 18:30\" — implying a change from an earlier time, but the original time isn''t stated. So I can''t say how much it moved. Worth flagging: check the original booking time / whether the connection still works.\n\nAlso note the Linkroom renewal already happened Oct 3 — no action needed, it said so.\n\nI should be concise. Also could offer to check calendar for the flight / add a reminder. Keep it short.\n\nShould I mention that the flight is in 3 days and the email is 7 weeks old — meaning it may have been missed. Yes.\n\nLet me answer."}],"createdAt":1793974995616},{"type":"text","text":"**The Northbeam Air schedule change** — it''s the only item with a deadline still ahead of it.\n\n**Northbeam Air — *Schedule change for booking NB7Q4K*** (Thu 17 Sep)\nFlight **NB 908, Frankfurt → Tokyo Haneda, Mon 9 Nov 2026** — that''s **three days from now**. It now departs **18:30** and arrives **14:15 the next day**; seat 14C is unchanged.\n\nWhy it outranks the rest:\n- It''s the only one of the five that is still in the future. The two Raj Mehta meetings (1 Oct and 8 Oct) and the Linkroom renewal (3 Oct) have all already passed.\n- The email is seven weeks old and unread-flagged as read, so the new departure time may never have made it into your plans.\n\nOne gap worth closing: the message says the flight \"now departs at 18:30\" but never states the original time, so I can''t tell you how much it moved or whether it breaks a connection. If you have the original booking confirmation, that''s the thing to compare against.\n\nThe others, for completeness: Linkroom explicitly said \"no action is needed\" and the USD 240 renewal has already gone through; the two meeting invitations are moot.\n\nWant me to check your calendar for 9 Nov to see whether the new 18:30 departure conflicts with anything, or search for the original NB7Q4K booking confirmation?","createdAt":1793974995616}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**The Northbeam Air schedule change** — it''s the only item with a deadline still ahead of it.\n\n**Northbeam Air — *Schedule change for booking NB7Q4K*** (Thu 17 Sep)\nFlight **NB 908, Frankfurt → Tokyo Haneda, Mon 9 Nov 2026** — that''s **three days from now**. It now departs **18:30** and arrives **14:15 the next day**; seat 14C is unchanged.\n\nWhy it outranks the rest:\n- It''s the only one of the five that is still in the future. The two Raj Mehta meetings (1 Oct and 8 Oct) and the Linkroom renewal (3 Oct) have all already passed.\n- The email is seven weeks old and unread-flagged as read, so the new departure time may never have made it into your plans.\n\nOne gap worth closing: the message says the flight \"now departs at 18:30\" but never states the original time, so I can''t tell you how much it moved or whether it breaks a connection. If you have the original booking confirmation, that''s the thing to compare against.\n\nThe others, for completeness: Linkroom explicitly said \"no action is needed\" and the USD 240 renewal has already gone through; the two meeting invitations are moot.\n\nWant me to check your calendar for 9 Nov to see whether the new 18:30 departure conflicts with anything, or search for the original NB7Q4K booking confirmation?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-06T14:23:04.389Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
