 client - Saffron & Sage).\n\nNote the discrepancy: the email invitation said \"Rebrand review\" but the calendar event is titled \"Design review\" at the same time. Worth flagging.\n\nAlso note: the kickoff was Oct 5, which was also a Portuguese holiday (Implantação da República) on Personal calendar — interesting but minor.\n\nAlso the query search only matched title presumably. Let me report:\n\n- Aozora rebrand kickoff — Work calendar, Mon 5 Oct 2026, 10:00–11:30 UTC, attendees Ana, Tomás Ortega, Kenji (aozora-ceramics.jp), location linkroom.app/r/aozora-kickoff. This is the event the \"Rebrand kickoff\" email refers to (email said start Oct 5).\n- Aozora logo review (internal) — Work, Thu 1 Oct, 14:00–15:00, Ana + Tomás, Studio 2. Matches the \"Updated invitation\" email.\n- Design review — Work, Thu 8 Oct, 15:00–16:00, Studio 2, no attendees listed. Same slot as the \"Rebrand review\" invitation from Raj (15:00–15:45). Likely the same meeting under a different title.\n- Kenji / Ana sync — Work, Fri 9 Oct, 08:00–08:30, linkroom.app/r/aozora.\n\nAll in the past. Nothing upcoming related to the rebrand — no future rebrand events at all in the window through Jan 2027.\n\nAlso note the kickoff overlapped with the Portuguese holiday on Personal calendar (5 Oct all-day) — minor, maybe mention briefly? It''s a nice detail but could be noise. I''ll mention it briefly as a footnote since it''s a real conflict signal. Actually it''s a public holiday in Portugal — the studio may have been closed. Worth one line.\n\nAlso note: no attendees include raj@demo.trymetis.email on the kickoff — Raj isn''t invited to the kickoff, though he''s the one who emailed about it. That''s a notable gap. Actually the kickoff attendees: ana, tomas, kenji. Raj not there. And the \"Design review\" Oct 8 has no attendees at all, while the email invitation from Raj listed it as an invite. Hmm, the email said \"Raj invited you to Rebrand review\" — so Ana is an attendee. The calendar event \"Design review\" has empty attendees. That''s a discrepancy worth flagging lightly.\n\nLet me write it up concisely.\n\nAlso should I mention the calendar names: all on \"Work\" calendar of ana@demo.trymetis.email.\n\nFormat: brief headline, then list.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The query \"rebrand\" returned one event: \"Aozora rebrand kickoff\" on Work calendar, Oct 5, 2026, 10:00–11:30 UTC, attendees ana, tomas, kenji@aozora-ceramics.jp, location linkroom.\n\nBut the full listing shows other related events that don''t have \"rebrand\" in the title but are clearly part of the same project: \"Aozora logo review (internal)\" Oct 1, \"Design review\" Oct 8 15:00 (which matches the \"Rebrand review\" invitation from Raj — the email said Rebrand review Thu Oct 8 15:00-15:45, and the calendar has \"Design review\" Oct 8 15:00-16:00 in Studio 2). Also \"Kenji / Ana sync\" Oct 9, \"Workshop: packaging prototypes\" Oct 8, \"Arabic menu proofs\" (different client - Saffron & Sage).\n\nNote the discrepancy: the email invitation said \"Rebrand review\" but the calendar event is titled \"Design review\" at the same time. Worth flagging.\n\nAlso note: the kickoff was Oct 5, which was also a Portuguese holiday (Implantação da República) on Personal calendar — interesting but minor.\n\nAlso the query search only matched title presumably. Let me report:\n\n- Aozora rebrand kickoff — Work calendar, Mon 5 Oct 2026, 10:00–11:30 UTC, attendees Ana, Tomás Ortega, Kenji (aozora-ceramics.jp), location linkroom.app/r/aozora-kickoff. This is the event the \"Rebrand kickoff\" email refers to (email said start Oct 5).\n- Aozora logo review (internal) — Work, Thu 1 Oct, 14:00–15:00, Ana + Tomás, Studio 2. Matches the \"Updated invitation\" email.\n- Design review — Work, Thu 8 Oct, 15:00–16:00, Studio 2, no attendees listed. Same slot as the \"Rebrand review\" invitation from Raj (15:00–15:45). Likely the same meeting under a different title.\n- Kenji / Ana sync — Work, Fri 9 Oct, 08:00–08:30, linkroom.app/r/aozora.\n\nAll in the past. Nothing upcoming related to the rebrand — no future rebrand events at all in the window through Jan 2027.\n\nAlso note the kickoff overlapped with the Portuguese holiday on Personal calendar (5 Oct all-day) — minor, maybe mention briefly? It''s a nice detail but could be noise. I''ll mention it briefly as a footnote since it''s a real conflict signal. Actually it''s a public holiday in Portugal — the studio may have been closed. Worth one line.\n\nAlso note: no attendees include raj@demo.trymetis.email on the kickoff — Raj isn''t invited to the kickoff, though he''s the one who emailed about it. That''s a notable gap. Actually the kickoff attendees: ana, tomas, kenji. Raj not there. And the \"Design review\" Oct 8 has no attendees at all, while the email invitation from Raj listed it as an invite. Hmm, the email said \"Raj invited you to Rebrand review\" — so Ana is an attendee. The calendar event \"Design review\" has empty attendees. That''s a discrepancy worth flagging lightly.\n\nLet me write it up concisely.\n\nAlso should I mention the calendar names: all on \"Work\" calendar of ana@demo.trymetis.email.\n\nFormat: brief headline, then list."}],"createdAt":1793975025594},{"type":"text","text":"**Yes — four events, all on the Work calendar of ana@demo.trymetis.email, and all in the past.** Nothing rebrand-related is scheduled from now through the end of January 2027.\n\n**Directly named:**\n- **Aozora rebrand kickoff** — Mon 5 Oct 2026, 10:00–11:30 UTC, `linkroom.app/r/aozora-kickoff`. Attendees: you, Tomás Ortega, kenji@aozora-ceramics.jp. This is the meeting the \"Rebrand kickoff\" email was setting up.\n\n**Same project, different titles:**\n- **Aozora logo review (internal)** — Thu 1 Oct 2026, 14:00–15:00 UTC, Studio 2. You and Tomás. Matches Raj''s \"Updated invitation\" email exactly.\n- **Design review** — Thu 8 Oct 2026, 15:00–16:00 UTC, Studio 2. Same slot as the \"Rebrand review\" Raj invited you to (15:00–15:45), but under a different name and with **no attendees listed** — so the calendar doesn''t corroborate that invitation.\n- **Kenji / Ana sync** — Fri 9 Oct 2026, 08:00–08:30 UTC, `linkroom.app/r/aozora`.\n\nThree things stand out:\n\n1. **Raj is not an attendee on the kickoff.** He''s the one who emailed you about starting the rebrand on 5 Oct, but the event lists only you, Tomás and Kenji.\n2. **The kickoff fell on a Portuguese public holiday** — *Implantação da República*, all day on your Personal calendar, 5 Oct. Worth knowing whether the studio was actually open.\n3. **The trail stops on 9 Oct.** No rebrand review, follow-up or next-phase event exists after that, which fits with the unanswered moodboard request in the email thread.\n\nWant me to check whether the moodboard or a reply went out from a folder I haven''t looked at, or draft a follow-up to Raj picking the project back up?","createdAt":1793975025594}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**Yes — four events, all on the Work calendar of ana@demo.trymetis.email, and all in the past.** Nothing rebrand-related is scheduled from now through the end of January 2027.\n\n**Directly named:**\n- **Aozora rebrand kickoff** — Mon 5 Oct 2026, 10:00–11:30 UTC, `linkroom.app/r/aozora-kickoff`. Attendees: you, Tomás Ortega, kenji@aozora-ceramics.jp. This is the meeting the \"Rebrand kickoff\" email was setting up.\n\n**Same project, different titles:**\n- **Aozora logo review (internal)** — Thu 1 Oct 2026, 14:00–15:00 UTC, Studio 2. You and Tomás. Matches Raj''s \"Updated invitation\" email exactly.\n- **Design review** — Thu 8 Oct 2026, 15:00–16:00 UTC, Studio 2. Same slot as the \"Rebrand review\" Raj invited you to (15:00–15:45), but under a different name and with **no attendees listed** — so the calendar doesn''t corroborate that invitation.\n- **Kenji / Ana sync** — Fri 9 Oct 2026, 08:00–08:30 UTC, `linkroom.app/r/aozora`.\n\nThree things stand out:\n\n1. **Raj is not an attendee on the kickoff.** He''s the one who emailed you about starting the rebrand on 5 Oct, but the event lists only you, Tomás and Kenji.\n2. **The kickoff fell on a Portuguese public holiday** — *Implantação da República*, all day on your Personal calendar, 5 Oct. Worth knowing whether the studio was actually open.\n3. **The trail stops on 9 Oct.** No rebrand review, follow-up or next-phase event exists after that, which fits with the unanswered moodboard request in the email thread.\n\nWant me to check whether the moodboard or a reply went out from a folder I haven''t looked at, or draft a follow-up to Raj picking the project back up?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-06T14:23:25.547Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
