e calendar. The email invitation from Raj said \"Rebrand review on Thu Oct 8, 2026, 15:00-15:45 UTC\". The calendar has \"Design review\" Thu 8 Oct 2026 15:00–16:00 UTC on the Work calendar, Studio 2, no attendees.\n\nSo the honest answer: there is no event named \"Rebrand review\" on any calendar. The closest is \"Design review\" on the Work calendar at 15:00–16:00 UTC on Thu 8 Oct 2026. The email said 15:00–15:45.\n\nI should be precise and flag the discrepancy. Also note it''s in the past (Oct 8, ~4 weeks ago).\n\nShould I re-verify? I already have the data from this conversation, freshly fetched. No need to re-query. But maybe a targeted query \"review\" would confirm there''s no \"Rebrand review\" event. The query \"rebrand\" returned only the kickoff. A query for \"review\" would return Design review, Monthly studio review, etc. I''m fairly confident. But to be safe and precise about \"no event named Rebrand review\", I could run a quick query \"review\" — cheap and confirms. Let me do it to be rigorous.\n\nActually, the full unfiltered listing over Sep 1 – Jan 31 was capped at 250 events and returned exactly 250 — meaning it was truncated! So the full listing is incomplete. But the query \"rebrand\" search is server-side and returned 1. A query \"review\" would be a targeted search. Let me run it to be thorough — it covers the whole window regardless of the 250 cap.\n\nLet me search query \"review\" over the same window."}],"createdAt":1793975031397},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"count":81,"events":[{"eventId":"http://caldav.localhost:5232/ana/work/monthly-review.ics#1788789600000","calendarAccountId":"ef21568e-53a9-597d-bc5c-451f8029a9de","accountEmail":"ana@demo.trymetis.email","calendarId":"http://caldav.localhost:5232/ana/work/","calendarName":"Work","title":"Monthly studio review","start":"2026-09-07T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-07T15:00:00.000Z","allDay":false,"location":"Studio 1","attendees":["ana@demo.trymet