type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"count":3,"emails":[{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","mailbox":"ana@demo.trymetis.email","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM2MF0","threadId":"<1c4quq9vn82woiuz@swiftpost.com>","from":"Swiftpost","subject":"Your Swiftpost parcel was delivered","date":"Tue Aug 04 2026 11:20:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":true,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""},{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","mailbox":"ana@demo.trymetis.email","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDMxNV0","threadId":"<3v78o0jmfo4h806b@swiftpost.com>","from":"Swiftpost","subject":"Your Swiftpost parcel was delivered","date":"Fri Apr 24 2026 12:55:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":true,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""},{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","mailbox":"ana@demo.trymetis.email","id":"WyJBcmNoaXZlIiwiMTAwMCIsMTBd","threadId":"<3rstfsq67b9a92ac@swiftpost.com>","from":"Swiftpost","subject":"Your Swiftpost parcel was delivered","date":"Thu Feb 13 2025 08:00:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":true,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""}]},"toolCallId":"call-1b6ef393-9d59-4d63-897b-63306e8c4e98","toolName":"searchMail","args":{"query":"delivered","mailboxId":null}},"updatedAt":1793975137494},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1793975137497,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Confirmed. Answer:\n\nMost recent shipment: order A-42, walnut desk lamp, Brightloom, shipped 23 Sep 2026 via Swiftpost, expected by 30 Sep. That''s 6.5 weeks ago — not \"recently\" in a strict sense.\n\nAnd critically: no delivery confirmation. The last Swiftpost \"delivered\" email is 4 Aug 2026 (for the earlier order A-38). So A-42 was expected by 30 Sep and there''s no delivered/out-for-delivery notice for it — 5+ weeks overdue with no tracking update in mail.\n\nAlso note: nothing shipped in the last few weeks at all. The only other order activity is marketing (Kestrel newsletter Sep 26).\n\nI should be careful: absence of a delivery email doesn''t prove non-delivery — the lamp may have arrived and Swiftpost just didn''t email, or it went to spam. I can''t see spam? searchMail searches every mailbox by default — but folders? It says searches connected mailboxes. I''ll caveat.\n\nLet me present.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed. Answer:\n\nMost recent shipment: order A-42, walnut desk lamp, Brightloom, shipped 23 Sep 2026 via Swiftpost, expected by 30 Sep. That''s 6.5 weeks ago — not \"recently\" in a strict sense.\n\nAnd critically: no delivery confirmation. The last Swiftpost \"delivered\" email is 4 Aug 2026 (for the earlier order A-38). So A-42 was expected by 30 Sep and there''s no delivered/out-for-delivery notice for it — 5+ weeks overdue with no tracking update in mail.\n\nAlso note: nothing shipped in the last few weeks at all. The only other order activity is marketing (Kestrel newsletter Sep 26).\n\nI should be careful: absence of a delivery email doesn''t prove non-delivery — the lamp may have arrived and Swiftpost just didn''t email, or it went to spam. I can''t see spam? searchMail searches every mailbox by default — but folders? It says searches connected mailboxes. I''ll caveat.\n\nLet me present."}],"createdAt":1793975144640},{"type":"text","text":"**Nothing has shipped in the last few weeks.** The most recent shipment on record is six and a half weeks old:\n\n- **Order A-42 — walnut desk lamp**, from Brightloom, shipped **Wed 23 Sep 2026** via Swiftpost, \"expected by September 30.\" Ordered 18 Sep.\n\nThat''s the only shipment since August. Before it, order A-38 went out 1 Aug and was delivered 4 Aug.\n\n**The part worth your attention: A-42 was due 30 Sep and there is no delivery confirmation for it.** Every other Swiftpost parcel in your mail has a matching \"out for delivery\" and \"delivered\" pair — A-38 on 4 Aug, the April order on 24 Apr, the Feb 2025 one. For A-42 the trail stops at \"on its way\" on 23 Sep. That''s five weeks past the expected date with no tracking update in your inbox.\n\nTwo honest caveats: a missing email doesn''t prove a missing lamp — it may have arrived with the notification going astray or landing in a folder I can''t see — and the \"track your package\" link in the Brightloom email is the only way to get the real status, since the message carries no tracking number in its text.\n\nWant me to draft a chase note to Brightloom about A-42, or search your spam and archive folders for a delivery notice first?","createdAt":1793975144640}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**Nothing has shipped in the last few weeks.** The most recent shipment on record is six and a half weeks old:\n\n- **Order A-42 — walnut desk lamp**, from Brightloom, shipped **Wed 23 Sep 2026** via Swiftpost, \"expected by September 30.\" Ordered 18 Sep.\n\nThat''s the only shipment since August. Before it, order A-38 went out 1 Aug and was delivered 4 Aug.\n\n**The part worth your attention: A-42 was due 30 Sep and there is no delivery confirmation for it.** Every other Swiftpost parcel in your mail has a matching \"out for delivery\" and \"delivered\" pair — A-38 on 4 Aug, the April order on 24 Apr, the Feb 2025 one. For A-42 the trail stops at \"on its way\" on 23 Sep. That''s five weeks past the expected date with no tracking update in your inbox.\n\nTwo honest caveats: a missing email doesn''t prove a missing lamp — it may have arrived with the notification going astray or landing in a folder I can''t see — and the \"track your package\" link in the Brightloom email is the only way to get the real status, since the message carries no tracking number in its text.\n\nWant me to draft a chase note to Brightloom about A-42, or search your spam and archive folders for a delivery notice first?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-06T14:25:16.621Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
