eaders\".\n\nLet me do: search_tools \"list attachments of an email\", search_tools \"email raw source links\".\n\nActually, getAttachmentText is loaded. I need listAttachments — search for it.\n\nLet me search both.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"I need to look for the tracking number. The Brightloom email said \"Track your package\" — likely a link with a tracking URL. The plain-text body may have stripped the URL. Let me check attachments? Or maybe there''s a tracking number in the email HTML. Let me try listAttachments for that email — maybe not.\n\nActually the getEmail returned plain text: \"Track your package\" with no URL shown (the link may have been truncated or the href not included). Let me see if there''s a tool to read email with links — maybe listAttachments won''t help. Let me search for a tool to get the email HTML/links, or check the Swiftpost \"on its way\" email of... wait, for A-42, the Swiftpost email? The Brightloom email says shipped with Swiftpost. There''s a Swiftpost email Aug 1 \"Your parcel from Brightloom is on its way\" — that''s for A-38.\n\nHmm, is there a Swiftpost email for A-42? Search results show Swiftpost emails: Sep 23 is from Brightloom (not Swiftpost). The Swiftpost emails are Aug 4 (x2), Aug 1, Jun 2 (from Ana, \"Swiftpost return\"), Apr 24, Apr 20, Apr 15, Oct 11 2025, Feb 13 2025. So no Swiftpost email for A-42 at all. Interesting — for A-38, Swiftpost sent both \"on its way\" (Aug 1) and \"out for delivery\"/\"delivered\" (Aug 4). For A-42, only Brightloom emailed.\n\nLet me try to get tracking details. Options:\n1. Read the raw email source / links — search for a tool.\n2. Check attachments of the A-42 email (maybe a tracking card).\n\nLet me search for tools: \"email links tracking number raw source\", \"list attachments email\".\n\nAlso there''s the \"Swiftpost return\" email from Ana on Jun 2 — might contain the tracking format. And the Apr 20 \"delayed\" email.\n\nLet me search tools for email attachments and maybe \"email headers\".\n\nLet me do: search_tools \"list attachments of an email\", search_tools \"email raw source links\".\n\nActually, getAttachmentText is loaded. I need listAttachments — search for it.\n\nLet me search both."}],"createdAt":1793975150818},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"results":[{"name":"listAttachments","description":"List the attachments on an email in a specific mailbox — attachmentId, filename, type and size.","score":13.44},{"name":"listFolder","description":"List the files and folders inside a folder of ONE specific drive. Omit folderId for the drive''s top level, then pass the fileId of a folder to go d...","score":8.75},{"name":"getEmail","description":"Fetch the full plain-text body of an email in a specific mailbox. Provide the mailboxId it belongs to.","score":6.63},{"name":"getRawEmail","description":"Fetch the raw source of an email in a specific mailbox — every header and MIME part. Use for delivery questions (Received, SPF, DKIM, DMARC, reply-...","score":6.19},{"name":"listMuted","description":"List the threadIds of the conversations you muted in a specific mailbox.","score":6.01}],"loaded":["listAttachments","listFolder","getEmail","getRawEmail","listMuted"],"message":"Found and loaded 5 tool(s): listAttachments, listFolder, getEmail, getRawEmail, listMuted. They are available on your next turn — call them directly. Some were already loaded."},"toolCallId":"call_e8e2f6ae8008465d8c41eff7","toolName":"search_tools","args":{"query":"list attachments of an email"}},"updatedAt":1793975150821},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"results":[{"name":"getRawEmail","description":"Fetch the raw source of an email in a specific mailbox — every header and MIME part. Use for delivery questions (Received, SPF, DKIM, DMARC, reply-...","score":14.08},{"name":"summarizeThread","description":"Summarize a conversation in a specific mailbox into cards — decisions, action ite