ug 4 out-for-delivery email references SP4471920385PT, that''s odd. Let me retry fetching it.\n\nLet me retry getEmail for ...359.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Now clearer:\n\nA-38 (July order): Swiftpost tracking numbers SP4471920368PT (shipped Aug 1), and the delivered one SP4471920402PT (delivered Aug 4). Hmm, two different numbers for A-38 — perhaps a different parcel or test data. Anyway.\n\nA-42: SP4471920385PT.\n\nThe Aug 4 06:30 \"out for delivery today\" email failed to fetch (transient error). It matched the search for SP4471920385PT — which is A-42''s number! That''s suspicious. If the Aug 4 out-for-delivery email references SP4471920385PT, that''s odd. Let me retry fetching it.\n\nLet me retry getEmail for ...359."}],"createdAt":1793975174844},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM1OV0","from":"Swiftpost","to":["ana@demo.trymetis.email"],"subject":"Your parcel is out for delivery today","date":"Tue Aug 04 2026 06:30:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","hasContent":true,"body":"Parcel SP4471920385PT for Brightloom order A-38: out for delivery . Your driver will arrive between 10:00 and 13:00. Track your parcel"},"toolCallId":"call_e03bb210e9b34c50b0cc7a4d","toolName":"getEmail","args":{"id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM1OV0","mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134"}},"updatedAt":1793975174851},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1793975174853,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Big finding: On 4 Aug 2026, Swiftpost said \"Parcel SP4471920385PT for Brightloom order A-38: out for delivery.\" Then the delivered email says \"Parcel SP4471920402PT for Brightloom order A-38: delivered.\"\n\nAnd Brightloom''s 23 Sep email for order A-42 quotes trackingNumber SP4471920385PT.\n\nSo SP4471920385PT was used on 4 Aug for order A-38, and again on 23 Sep for order A-42. Either:\n(a) Brightloom reused/duplicated the tracking number in its A-42 email (a copy/paste error), or\n(b) the number was genuinely recycled.\n\nNote also A-38 had two numbers itself: 368PT (shipped) and 402PT (delivered) and 385PT (out for delivery). Three different numbers all labelled \"order A-38\". That''s messy — the Swiftpost notices for A-38 carry inconsistent tracking numbers.\n\nSo the tracking situation for A-42:\n- Only one record: Brightloom''s own \"shipped\" email, dated 23 Sep 2026, with tracking number SP4471920385PT and URL https://swiftpost.com/track/SP4471920385PT.\n- Swiftpost itself never emailed about A-42 — no shipped/out-for-delivery/delivered notice from the carrier, unlike A-38 which had three Swiftpost notices.\n- The number Brightloom gave for A-42 is the same number Swiftpost used on 4 Aug for A-38''s out-for-delivery notice, so it may not reliably identify the lamp.\n- The structured shipment card shows status \"shipped\", deliveredAt null, expectedAt 2026-09-30T20:00:00Z — five weeks past, still not marked delivered.\n- No attachment, no separate tracking document.\n\nAlso the tracking link was invisible in the plain-text version of the email — the href only exists in the HTML — so if you were reading it as text you''d never have seen the URL.\n\nSo: I cannot fetch the live status from swiftpost.com/track — I have no web tool. Let me check whether I have a tool to check tracking? Probably not. I could mention that. Should I search tools for \"track parcel status\"? It''s a reasonable search. Let me try one search to be thorough.\n\nActually, is there a possibility the workspace has a parcel-tracking tool? Let me search \"parcel tracking status package\" once.\n\nI''ll do it.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Big finding: On 4 Aug 2026, Swiftpost said \"Parcel SP4471920385PT for Brightloom order A-38: out for delivery.\" Then the delivered email says \"Parcel SP4471920402PT for Brightloom order A-38: delivered.\"\n\nAnd Brightloom''s 23 Sep email for order A-42 quotes trackingNumber SP4471920385PT.\n\nSo SP4471920385PT was used on 4 Aug for order A-38, and again on 23 Sep for order A-42. Either:\n(a) Brightloom reused/duplicated the tracking number in its A-42 email (a copy/paste error), or\n(b) the number was genuinely recycled.\n\nNote also A-38 had two numbers itself: 368PT (shipped) and 402PT (delivered) and 385PT (out for delivery). Three different numbers all labelled \"order A-38\". That''s messy — the Swiftpost notices for A-38 carry inconsistent tracking numbers.\n\nSo the tracking situation for A-42:\n- Only one record: Brightloom''s own \"shipped\" email, dated 23 Sep 2026, with tracking number SP4471920385PT and URL https://swiftpost.com/track/SP4471920385PT.\n- Swiftpost itself never emailed about A-42 — no shipped/out-for-delivery/delivered notice from the carrier, unlike A-38 which had three Swiftpost notices.\n- The number Brightloom gave for A-42 is the same number Swiftpost used on 4 Aug for A-38''s out-for-delivery notice, so it may not reliably identify the lamp.\n- The structured shipment card shows status \"shipped\", deliveredAt null, expectedAt 2026-09-30T20:00:00Z — five weeks past, still not marked delivered.\n- No attachment, no separate tracking document.\n\nAlso the tracking link was invisible in the plain-text version of the email — the href only exists in the HTML — so if you were reading it as text you''d never have seen the URL.\n\nSo: I cannot fetch the live status from swiftpost.com/track — I have no web tool. Let me check whether I have a tool to check tracking? Probably not. I could mention that. Should I search tools for \"track parcel status\"? It''s a reasonable search. Let me try one search to be thorough.\n\nActually, is there a possibility the workspace has a parcel-tracking tool? Let me search \"parcel tracking status package\" once.\n\nI''ll do it."}],"createdAt":1793975180329},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"results":[{"name":"getRawEmail","description":"Fetch the raw source of an email in a specific mailbox — every header and MIME part. Use for delivery questions (Received, SPF, DKIM, DMARC, reply-...","score":4.71},{"name":"listScheduled","description":"List the scheduled emails in a specific mailbox — when each goes out, its status, subject and recipients.","score":4.24},{"name":"listWorkflowRuns","description":"List recent workflow runs in this workspace — status, attempts, per-step outcomes and any error. Use to review what the automation actually did.","score":3.82}],"loaded":["getRawEmail","listScheduled","listWorkflowRuns"],"message":"Found and loaded 3 tool(s): getRawEmail, listScheduled, listWorkflowRuns. They are available on your next turn — call them directly. Some were already loaded."},"toolCallId":"call_7e32454cb7f840cc869da488","toolName":"search_tools","args":{"query":"track parcel shipment status package delivery"}},"updatedAt":1793975180331},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1793975180334,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"No live tracking tool. So I report what mail holds.\n\nWrite up the tracking situation.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"No live tracking tool. So I report what mail holds.\n\nWrite up the tracking situation."}],"createdAt":1793975188066},{"type":"text","text":"Here''s the full tracking picture for order A-42. It comes out of the HTML source of the Brightloom email, and there are problems with it.\n\n**The number Brightloom gave you**\n- Carrier: **Swiftpost**\n- Tracking number: **`SP4471920385PT`**\n- URL: `https://swiftpost.com/track/SP4471920385PT`\n- Expected arrival: **2026-09-30 20:00 UTC**\n- Item: walnut desk lamp, order A-42, merchant Brightloom\n\n**Three things are wrong with that**\n\n1. **The number is already spent.** Swiftpost used `SP4471920385PT` on **4 Aug 2026** for a *different* order: \"Parcel SP4471920385PT for Brightloom order **A-38**: out for delivery. Your driver will arrive between 10:00 and 13:00.\" Brightloom''s September email re-issues the same number for A-42. Either Brightloom copy-pasted the old tracking ID into the new shipping notice, or the number was recycled — either way it does not reliably point at your lamp. Track that link and you may be reading the status of a parcel delivered in August.\n\n2. **Swiftpost itself never wrote to you about A-42.** For order A-38 the carrier sent three separate notices — shipped (1 Aug), out for delivery (4 Aug), delivered (4 Aug). For A-42 there is **no Swiftpost email at all**. The only record of the shipment anywhere in your mail is Brightloom''s own notice. So no independent carrier confirmation exists that the lamp ever left, let alone arrived.\n\n3. **The status card still says \"shipped\", with no delivery date.** The structured shipment record inside the email reads `status: shipped`, `deliveredAt: null`, `expectedAt: 2026-09-30T20:00Z`. Nothing has updated it in the five weeks since the expected date.\n\n**One more wrinkle:** the tracking link is only in the HTML part of the email. In the plain-text body it''s just the words \"Track your package\" with no URL — so if you read that mail as text, the tracking number was never visible to you at all.\n\n**What I can''t do:** I have no way to pull live status from Swiftpost — no web access from here, and no parcel-tracking tool in this workspace. The only authoritative check is opening `https://swiftpost.com/track/SP4471920385PT` yourself, and even then I''d treat the result sceptically given the number collision with A-38.\n\nMy reading: this is not a parcel sitting in a depot — it''s a shipment with a **corroboration gap**. One merchant email, a tracking number shared with an older order, and no carrier side. Worth asking Brightloom for the lamp''s actual consignment ID rather than chasing the one you were given. Want me to draft that email?","createdAt":1793975188066}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"Here''s the full tracking picture for order A-42. It comes out of the HTML source of the Brightloom email, and there are problems with it.\n\n**The number Brightloom gave you**\n- Carrier: **Swiftpost**\n- Tracking number: **`SP4471920385PT`**\n- URL: `https://swiftpost.com/track/SP4471920385PT`\n- Expected arrival: **2026-09-30 20:00 UTC**\n- Item: walnut desk lamp, order A-42, merchant Brightloom\n\n**Three things are wrong with that**\n\n1. **The number is already spent.** Swiftpost used `SP4471920385PT` on **4 Aug 2026** for a *different* order: \"Parcel SP4471920385PT for Brightloom order **A-38**: out for delivery. Your driver will arrive between 10:00 and 13:00.\" Brightloom''s September email re-issues the same number for A-42. Either Brightloom copy-pasted the old tracking ID into the new shipping notice, or the number was recycled — either way it does not reliably point at your lamp. Track that link and you may be reading the status of a parcel delivered in August.\n\n2. **Swiftpost itself never wrote to you about A-42.** For order A-38 the carrier sent three separate notices — shipped (1 Aug), out for delivery (4 Aug), delivered (4 Aug). For A-42 there is **no Swiftpost email at all**. The only record of the shipment anywhere in your mail is Brightloom''s own notice. So no independent carrier confirmation exists that the lamp ever left, let alone arrived.\n\n3. **The status card still says \"shipped\", with no delivery date.** The structured shipment record inside the email reads `status: shipped`, `deliveredAt: null`, `expectedAt: 2026-09-30T20:00Z`. Nothing has updated it in the five weeks since the expected date.\n\n**One more wrinkle:** the tracking link is only in the HTML part of the email. In the plain-text body it''s just the words \"Track your package\" with no URL — so if you read that mail as text, the tracking number was never visible to you at all.\n\n**What I can''t do:** I have no way to pull live status from Swiftpost — no web access from here, and no parcel-tracking tool in this workspace. The only authoritative check is opening `https://swiftpost.com/track/SP4471920385PT` yourself, and even then I''d treat the result sceptically given the number collision with A-38.\n\nMy reading: this is not a parcel sitting in a depot — it''s a shipment with a **corroboration gap**. One merchant email, a tracking number shared with an older order, and no carrier side. Worth asking Brightloom for the lamp''s actual consignment ID rather than chasing the one you were given. Want me to draft that email?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-06T14:25:50.818Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
