w that abruptly stopped.\n\nAlso worth noting the \"Not you? Call 1800 266 4821\" — standard. No suspicious activity flagged. Actually the abrupt stop of debits could be benign (e.g., they moved banks) or could mean alerts stopped arriving. Worth flagging as a check, not alarm.\n\nAlso note: the alerts are read, nothing unread/flagged.\n\nNote the language detail: the July alert came in Hindi, so it was invisible to an English-only keyword search — worth mentioning since it shows a search gap.\n\nFormat: markdown. One-line headline, then table.\n\nCareful not to overstate. I''ll present.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a good picture. Let me assemble.\n\nOnly one mailbox: ana@demo.trymetis.email. All bank alerts from Konkan Bank, account **4821.\n\nDebits, newest first, with payee:\n- 25 Sep 2026 — INR 1,250.00 — chaiwala.store@konkan — UPI Ref 427311009876 — balance 48,210.55\n- 12 Sep 2026 — INR 450.00 — chaiwala.store@konkan — balance 49,460.55\n- 2 Aug 2026 — INR 2,760.00 — tavola.mumbai@upi — balance 52,833.70\n- 19 Jul 2026 — INR 3,100.00 — kestrelsupply@upi — balance 57,212.30 (Hindi-language alert)\n- 8 Jun 2026 — INR 980.00 — metro.pune@upi — balance 60,072.40\n- 17 Apr 2026 — INR 6,300.00 — swiftpost.in@upi — refunded in full 29 Apr (INR 6,300.00 credited)\n- 4 Feb 2026 — INR 1,260.00 — chaiwala.store@konkan — balance 71,402.90\n- older ones in archive: 19 Dec 2025 (4,200), 9 Oct 2025 (2,150), 26 Aug 2025 (7,850), 11 Jul 2025 (540), 30 May 2025 (3,480), 3 Apr 2025 (1,099), 20 Feb 2025 (12,500), 14 Jan 2025 (860), 28 Nov 2024 (2,340)\n\nHeadline: No money has left the account in the last six weeks — nothing since 25 Sep 2026. And nothing at all in October or November.\n\nBalance trend: 71,402.90 (Feb) → 60,072.40 (Jun) → 57,212.30 (Jul) → 52,833.70 (Aug) → 49,460.55 (Sep 12) → 48,210.55 (Sep 25). Steady decline, then nothing.\n\nPatterns worth noting:\n- chaiwala.store@konkan appears three times: 1,260 (Feb), 450 (Sep 12), 1,250 (Sep 25). A food/tea place — looks like a habit, but irregular amounts.\n- The 6,300 swiftpost.in debit was refunded in full 12 days later.\n- 15 debits over ~2 years; the largest was 12,500 in Feb 2025.\n- Only one credit in the whole set: the swiftpost refund.\n\nTotal in the \"lately\" window — ambiguous. I''ll define windows: last 6 weeks (since 25 Sep, i.e., nothing), last 90 days (since ~8 Aug): 25 Sep 1,250 + 12 Sep 450 + 2 Aug... wait 2 Aug is outside 90 days? 8 Aug to 6 Nov is 90 days. 2 Aug is 96 days ago. So last 90 days ≈ 1,700. Let me be careful: 6 Nov minus 90 days = 8 Aug 2026. So debits since 8 Aug: 25 Sep (1,250) + 12 Sep (450) = 1,700.\n\nLast 6 months (since 6 May 2026): 25 Sep 1,250 + 12 Sep 450 + 2 Aug 2,760 + 19 Jul 3,100 + 8 Jun 980 = 8,540.\n\nLet me present clearly with the \"lately\" framing: nothing in six weeks. That itself is the finding — a steady out-flow that abruptly stopped.\n\nAlso worth noting the \"Not you? Call 1800 266 4821\" — standard. No suspicious activity flagged. Actually the abrupt stop of debits could be benign (e.g., they moved banks) or could mean alerts stopped arriving. Worth flagging as a check, not alarm.\n\nAlso note: the alerts are read, nothing unread/flagged.\n\nNote the language detail: the July alert came in Hindi, so it was invisible to an English-only keyword search — worth mentioning since it shows a search gap.\n\nFormat: markdown. One-line headline, then table.\n\nCareful not to overstate. I''ll present."}],"createdAt":1793975230803},{"type":"text","text":"**One mailbox, one account, and the striking thing is the silence: nothing has left it in six weeks.** All the financial mail is Konkan Bank alerts for account **4821 in ana@demo.trymetis.email** — that''s the only connected mailbox, and there are no other banks, cards or payment services in the workspace.\n\n**Recent debits (newest first)**\n\n| Date | Amount | Paid to | Balance after |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 25 Sep 2026 | INR 1,250.00 | `chaiwala.store@konkan` | 48,210.55 |\n| 12 Sep 2026 | INR 450.00 | `chaiwala.store@konkan` | 49,460.55 |\n| 2 Aug 2026 | INR 2,760.00 | `tavola.mumbai@upi` | 52,833.70 |\n| 19 Jul 2026 | INR 3,100.00 | `kestrelsupply@upi` | 57,212.30 |\n| 8 Jun 2026 | INR 980.00 | `metro.pune@upi` | 60,072.40 |\n| 17 Apr 2026 | INR 6,300.00 | `swiftpost.in@upi` | 55,610.15 |\n| 4 Feb 2026 | INR 1,260.00 | `chaiwala.store@konkan` | 71,402.90 |\n\nEverything before February 2026 sits in your archive — nine further debits going back to Nov 2024, the largest being **INR 12,500.00 on 20 Feb 2025**.\n\n**What the numbers say**\n\n- **Nothing at all in October or November.** The last transaction of any kind was 25 Sep, and that''s the *only* movement recorded since mid-September. Six weeks of complete stillness on an account that had been debiting every three to eight weeks for two years.\n- **The out-goings were small, recurring and habitual** — INR 1,700 total in the last 90 days, 8,540 over the last six months. `chaiwala.store@konkan` has hit the account three times (Feb, Sep 12, Sep 25), which reads more like a tea-and-food habit than a subscription, since the amounts vary.\n- **The balance was draining steadily** — 71,402 in February down to 48,210 by late September, about INR 23,000 over seven months. Then flat.\n- **One credit exists in the entire history: the 6,300 refund.** On 17 Apr you paid `swiftpost.in@upi` INR 6,300, and it came back in full on 29 Apr marked \"(refund)\". Every other transaction in the record is money leaving.\n\n**Two caveats you should hear before you act on this.** First, the July debit arrived in **Hindi** (\"खाता **4821 से INR 3,100.00 डेबिट\") while the rest are English — it doesn''t match an English keyword search, and if your own filtering relies on English terms you''d have missed it too. Second, an absence of alerts is not proof the account is idle — it could just as easily mean **the alerts stopped arriving**, so I''d verify the silence is real with the bank rather than treating this list as a complete ledger. Nothing here looks fraudulent; no card-present charges, no new payees, and the only unrecognised-looking names are a restaurant and a metro card.\n\nWant me to draft a note to the bank confirming your alert settings are still live, or a workflow that flags any debit over a threshold going forward?","createdAt":1793975230803}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**One mailbox, one account, and the striking thing is the silence: nothing has left it in six weeks.** All the financial mail is Konkan Bank alerts for account **4821 in ana@demo.trymetis.email** — that''s the only connected mailbox, and there are no other banks, cards or payment services in the workspace.\n\n**Recent debits (newest first)**\n\n| Date | Amount | Paid to | Balance after |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 25 Sep 2026 | INR 1,250.00 | `chaiwala.store@konkan` | 48,210.55 |\n| 12 Sep 2026 | INR 450.00 | `chaiwala.store@konkan` | 49,460.55 |\n| 2 Aug 2026 | INR 2,760.00 | `tavola.mumbai@upi` | 52,833.70 |\n| 19 Jul 2026 | INR 3,100.00 | `kestrelsupply@upi` | 57,212.30 |\n| 8 Jun 2026 | INR 980.00 | `metro.pune@upi` | 60,072.40 |\n| 17 Apr 2026 | INR 6,300.00 | `swiftpost.in@upi` | 55,610.15 |\n| 4 Feb 2026 | INR 1,260.00 | `chaiwala.store@konkan` | 71,402.90 |\n\nEverything before February 2026 sits in your archive — nine further debits going back to Nov 2024, the largest being **INR 12,500.00 on 20 Feb 2025**.\n\n**What the numbers say**\n\n- **Nothing at all in October or November.** The last transaction of any kind was 25 Sep, and that''s the *only* movement recorded since mid-September. Six weeks of complete stillness on an account that had been debiting every three to eight weeks for two years.\n- **The out-goings were small, recurring and habitual** — INR 1,700 total in the last 90 days, 8,540 over the last six months. `chaiwala.store@konkan` has hit the account three times (Feb, Sep 12, Sep 25), which reads more like a tea-and-food habit than a subscription, since the amounts vary.\n- **The balance was draining steadily** — 71,402 in February down to 48,210 by late September, about INR 23,000 over seven months. Then flat.\n- **One credit exists in the entire history: the 6,300 refund.** On 17 Apr you paid `swiftpost.in@upi` INR 6,300, and it came back in full on 29 Apr marked \"(refund)\". Every other transaction in the record is money leaving.\n\n**Two caveats you should hear before you act on this.** First, the July debit arrived in **Hindi** (\"खाता **4821 से INR 3,100.00 डेबिट\") while the rest are English — it doesn''t match an English keyword search, and if your own filtering relies on English terms you''d have missed it too. Second, an absence of alerts is not proof the account is idle — it could just as easily mean **the alerts stopped arriving**, so I''d verify the silence is real with the bank rather than treating this list as a complete ledger. Nothing here looks fraudulent; no card-present charges, no new payees, and the only unrecognised-looking names are a restaurant and a metro card.\n\nWant me to draft a note to the bank confirming your alert settings are still live, or a workflow that flags any debit over a threshold going forward?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-06T14:26:35.090Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
