hill Studio weekly: from \"weekly\" search: Sep 14 2026, Jul 13 2026, May 11 2026, Feb 9 2026, Nov 10 2025, Sep 15 2025, Jul 14 2025, May 12 2025, Mar 10 2025, Jan 13 2025 = 10. These are internal team digests from Priya Nair — arguably a digest but internal, not a newsletter.\n\nLet me also check Linkroom and other promotional. Let me do one more search for \"sale\" / \"off\" to catch promotional, and \"Linkroom\".\n\nActually, I should be careful about scope creep. The user asked to \"find emails that look like newsletters or digests.\" I should give a categorized list with counts and note the label option.\n\nLet me do a couple more searches to be complete: \"Linkroom\", \"sale\", \"off this weekend\".\n\nActually let me search \"unsubscribe\" alone — returned 0 combined with newsletter. Let me try \"unsubscribe\" alone, and \"sale\".\n\nLet me batch: \"unsubscribe\", \"sale\", \"Linkroom\", \"Paperstack month\".\n\nHmm, \"Paperstack month\" would confirm count. Let me do it.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"I have a good picture. Let me also check for other marketing/promotional senders: Linkroom (\"Linkroom for teams: shared recordings\", \"Breakout rooms are here\"), Voltaro Energy bill (not newsletter), Kestrel \"15% off this weekend only\" and \"Spring sale starts now\" (promotional, not newsletter).\n\nLet me search \"off this weekend\" / \"sale\" to catch promotional ones, and maybe \"Paperstack month\" already covered.\n\nActually the user asked for \"newsletters or digests\". I should distinguish:\n- True recurring newsletters/digests: Kestrel \"This week at Kestrel\" (weekly), Codeyard \"Your weekly Codeyard digest\" (weekly), Paperstack \"Your Paperstack month\" (monthly), Fernhill \"Studio weekly\" (internal, from Priya — a team digest, arguably).\n- Promotional one-offs: Kestrel \"15% off this weekend only\", \"Spring sale starts now\", Linkroom product announcements.\n\nLet me count Kestrel \"This week at\" — the search returned 56 results for \"t