ck","subject":"Your Paperstack month: March 2026","date":"Mon Mar 02 2026 09:00:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":true,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""},{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","mailbox":"ana@demo.trymetis.email","id":"WyJBcmNoaXZlIiwiMTAwMCIsNjFd","threadId":"<41izi9iirqtnnz8b@paperstack.app>","from":"Paperstack","subject":"Your Paperstack month: January 2026","date":"Fri Jan 02 2026 09:00:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":true,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""},{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","mailbox":"ana@demo.trymetis.email","id":"WyJBcmNoaXZlIiwiMTAwMCIsNDld","threadId":"<4i5s6imuox7j3es5@paperstack.app>","from":"Paperstack","subject":"Your Paperstack month: November 2025","date":"Sun Nov 02 2025 09:00:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":true,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""}]},"toolCallId":"call-355b3b45-4380-4b00-87e6-c6f5433bddaf","toolName":"searchMail","args":{"query":"Paperstack month","mailboxId":null}},"updatedAt":1793975321441},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1793975321444,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Now I have a solid picture. Let me tally.\n\n**Recurring newsletters/digests (bulk, unsubscribe-bearing):**\n\n1. Kestrel Supply Co. — \"This week at Kestrel: ...\" weekly. Count from \"this week at\" search: 56 results, all Kestrel. Includes \"This week at the shop\" (Sep 26). So 56 total Kestrel weekly sends. Let me verify: the \"this week at\" search returned count 56 and all were Kestrel. Yes.\n\n2. Codeyard — \"Your weekly Codeyard digest\": 5 (Sep 7, Aug 24, Jul 27, Jun 29, Jun 1 2026).\n\n3. Paperstack — \"Your Paperstack month: <Month> <Year>\": 6 (Nov 2025, Jan, Mar, May, Jul, Sep 2026). Every other month.\n\n4. Fernhill Studio weekly (from Priya Nair) — 10: Jan 13 2025, Mar 10 2025, May 12 2025, Jul 14 2025, Sep 15 2025, Nov 10 2025, Feb 9 2026, May 11 2026, Jul 13 2026, Sep 14 2026. Internal team digest — not a marketing newsletter, but a digest in form.\n\n**Promotional / product-announcement bulk mail (newsletter-adjacent, not digests):**\n- Kestrel: \"15% off this weekend only\" (14 Aug 2026), \"Spring sale starts now\" (20 Mar 2026)\n- Linkroom: \"Linkroom for teams: shared recordings\" (8 Sep 2026), \"Breakout rooms are here\" (21 Apr 2026), \"Linkroom rooms now remember your layout\" (23 Sep 2025), \"New in Linkroom: live captions in 12 languages\" (18 Feb 2025)\n- Northbeam Air: \"Fly to Osaka from Frankfurt, new route from October\" (16 Jun 2026), \"Summer in Lisbon: city breaks from EUR 79\" (10 Jun 2025)\n- Tavola: \"You''re unsubscribed from Tavola picks\" (7 Mar 2026) — evidence of a \"Tavola picks\" newsletter that was unsubscribed; the newsletter itself isn''t in the mailbox.\n\nTotal: 56 + 5 + 6 + 10 = 77 recurring digests. Plus 8 promotional.\n\nHmm, let me double check the Kestrel count of 56. The \"this week at\" search returned count 56. But wait — does that include \"This week at the shop\"? Yes, first result. So 56 Kestrel weekly emails.\n\nBut careful: the search may be capped. count: 56 with 56 items listed? I didn''t count the list. Let me trust count.\n\nActually, let me sanity check: Kestrel weekly from Nov 2024 to Sep 2026 ≈ 96 weeks. Only 56 present. Fine — the mailbox doesn''t have every one.\n\nAlso note: the \"unsubscribe\" search returned 71 — that''s the union of Kestrel (56) + Linkroom (4) + Northbeam (2) + Tavola (1) + Codeyard (5) + Paperstack (6) + ... let''s see: 56+5+6+4+2+1 = 74. Hmm, 71. Close enough; some may not contain \"unsubscribe\". Actually the unsubscribe search returned 71 items and included Kestrel, Linkroom, Codeyard, Paperstack, Northbeam, Tavola. Let me not over-claim exact per-sender from that.\n\nLet me be careful with numbers I state. I''ll state:\n- Kestrel: 56 (from \"this week at\" search)\n- Codeyard: 5\n- Paperstack: 6\n- Fernhill Studio weekly: 10\n- Linkroom: 4 product announcements\n- Northbeam Air: 2 route/promo\n- Kestrel promos: 2\n- Tavola: 1 unsubscribe confirmation\n\nTotal recurring digests: 77. Total bulk/newsletter-shaped: 77 + 8 = 85, plus the Tavola unsubscribe notice.\n\nHmm, but is \"Fernhill Studio weekly\" a newsletter? It''s an internal team digest from Priya. I''ll categorize it separately as \"internal digest\" — it''s a digest in form but not bulk mail.\n\nSo: 67 external newsletter/digest emails (56+5+6), 10 internal digests, 8 promotional.\n\nLet me present with a table, note the label option (`newsletter` and `promotional` built-ins exist), and offer to apply labels.\n\nAlso worth noting: none of these are unread — all read. And the Kestrel cadence: weekly, but the last one is 26 Sep 2026 — six weeks ago, consistent with the general silence in this mailbox since late September.\n\nInteresting observation: everything in this mailbox stops around 26 Sep 2026. That''s a pattern across all three questions. Worth a brief note.\n\nLet me write it up.\n\nAlso I should mention the \"newsletter\" label exists and I could apply it. Offer.\n\nLet me count Kestrel promos: \"15% off this weekend only\" (Aug 14 2026), \"Spring sale starts now\" (Mar 20 2026). Yes 2.\n\nLinkroom: 4 (Sep 8 2026, Apr 21 2026, Sep 23 2025, Feb 18 2025). Plus \"Your Linkroom Pro plan renews on October 3\" (billing, not newsletter) and \"Confirm your email for Linkroom\" (transactional).\n\nNorthbeam: 2 marketing (Jun 16 2026, Jun 10 2025). Plus booking confirmations/schedule change (transactional).\n\nGood. Write it.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a solid picture. Let me tally.\n\n**Recurring newsletters/digests (bulk, unsubscribe-bearing):**\n\n1. Kestrel Supply Co. — \"This week at Kestrel: ...\" weekly. Count from \"this week at\" search: 56 results, all Kestrel. Includes \"This week at the shop\" (Sep 26). So 56 total Kestrel weekly sends. Let me verify: the \"this week at\" search returned count 56 and all were Kestrel. Yes.\n\n2. Codeyard — \"Your weekly Codeyard digest\": 5 (Sep 7, Aug 24, Jul 27, Jun 29, Jun 1 2026).\n\n3. Paperstack — \"Your Paperstack month: <Month> <Year>\": 6 (Nov 2025, Jan, Mar, May, Jul, Sep 2026). Every other month.\n\n4. Fernhill Studio weekly (from Priya Nair) — 10: Jan 13 2025, Mar 10 2025, May 12 2025, Jul 14 2025, Sep 15 2025, Nov 10 2025, Feb 9 2026, May 11 2026, Jul 13 2026, Sep 14 2026. Internal team digest — not a marketing newsletter, but a digest in form.\n\n**Promotional / product-announcement bulk mail (newsletter-adjacent, not digests):**\n- Kestrel: \"15% off this weekend only\" (14 Aug 2026), \"Spring sale starts now\" (20 Mar 2026)\n- Linkroom: \"Linkroom for teams: shared recordings\" (8 Sep 2026), \"Breakout rooms are here\" (21 Apr 2026), \"Linkroom rooms now remember your layout\" (23 Sep 2025), \"New in Linkroom: live captions in 12 languages\" (18 Feb 2025)\n- Northbeam Air: \"Fly to Osaka from Frankfurt, new route from October\" (16 Jun 2026), \"Summer in Lisbon: city breaks from EUR 79\" (10 Jun 2025)\n- Tavola: \"You''re unsubscribed from Tavola picks\" (7 Mar 2026) — evidence of a \"Tavola picks\" newsletter that was unsubscribed; the newsletter itself isn''t in the mailbox.\n\nTotal: 56 + 5 + 6 + 10 = 77 recurring digests. Plus 8 promotional.\n\nHmm, let me double check the Kestrel count of 56. The \"this week at\" search returned count 56. But wait — does that include \"This week at the shop\"? Yes, first result. So 56 Kestrel weekly emails.\n\nBut careful: the search may be capped. count: 56 with 56 items listed? I didn''t count the list. Let me trust count.\n\nActually, let me sanity check: Kestrel weekly from Nov 2024 to Sep 2026 ≈ 96 weeks. Only 56 present. Fine — the mailbox doesn''t have every one.\n\nAlso note: the \"unsubscribe\" search returned 71 — that''s the union of Kestrel (56) + Linkroom (4) + Northbeam (2) + Tavola (1) + Codeyard (5) + Paperstack (6) + ... let''s see: 56+5+6+4+2+1 = 74. Hmm, 71. Close enough; some may not contain \"unsubscribe\". Actually the unsubscribe search returned 71 items and included Kestrel, Linkroom, Codeyard, Paperstack, Northbeam, Tavola. Let me not over-claim exact per-sender from that.\n\nLet me be careful with numbers I state. I''ll state:\n- Kestrel: 56 (from \"this week at\" search)\n- Codeyard: 5\n- Paperstack: 6\n- Fernhill Studio weekly: 10\n- Linkroom: 4 product announcements\n- Northbeam Air: 2 route/promo\n- Kestrel promos: 2\n- Tavola: 1 unsubscribe confirmation\n\nTotal recurring digests: 77. Total bulk/newsletter-shaped: 77 + 8 = 85, plus the Tavola unsubscribe notice.\n\nHmm, but is \"Fernhill Studio weekly\" a newsletter? It''s an internal team digest from Priya. I''ll categorize it separately as \"internal digest\" — it''s a digest in form but not bulk mail.\n\nSo: 67 external newsletter/digest emails (56+5+6), 10 internal digests, 8 promotional.\n\nLet me present with a table, note the label option (`newsletter` and `promotional` built-ins exist), and offer to apply labels.\n\nAlso worth noting: none of these are unread — all read. And the Kestrel cadence: weekly, but the last one is 26 Sep 2026 — six weeks ago, consistent with the general silence in this mailbox since late September.\n\nInteresting observation: everything in this mailbox stops around 26 Sep 2026. That''s a pattern across all three questions. Worth a brief note.\n\nLet me write it up.\n\nAlso I should mention the \"newsletter\" label exists and I could apply it. Offer.\n\nLet me count Kestrel promos: \"15% off this weekend only\" (Aug 14 2026), \"Spring sale starts now\" (Mar 20 2026). Yes 2.\n\nLinkroom: 4 (Sep 8 2026, Apr 21 2026, Sep 23 2025, Feb 18 2025). Plus \"Your Linkroom Pro plan renews on October 3\" (billing, not newsletter) and \"Confirm your email for Linkroom\" (transactional).\n\nNorthbeam: 2 marketing (Jun 16 2026, Jun 10 2025). Plus booking confirmations/schedule change (transactional).\n\nGood. Write it."}],"createdAt":1793975344176},{"type":"text","text":"**67 external newsletter/digest emails, from three senders — plus 10 internal digests and 8 promotional blasts.** All of them are read, and all sit in ana@demo.trymetis.email.\n\n**Recurring newsletters and digests**\n\n| Sender | Pattern | Count | Cadence | Latest |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Kestrel Supply Co.** | \"This week at Kestrel: …\" | 56 | weekly | 26 Sep 2026 |\n| **Paperstack** | \"Your Paperstack month: <Month>\" | 6 | every other month | 2 Sep 2026 |\n| **Codeyard** | \"Your weekly Codeyard digest\" | 5 | weekly | 7 Sep 2026 |\n\nKestrel is by far the dominant one — 56 sends going back to Nov 2024, cycling through the same five subjects (\"A kitchen for slow mornings\", \"The candle edit\", \"Stoneware from Porto\", \"Gifts under EUR 30\", \"Notebooks for the new year\", plus \"Meet the maker: Oficina Lume\" and one \"Workshop: kintsugi basics\"). It''s a shop newsletter with a fixed rotation.\n\nPaperstack is the odd one: it calls itself a monthly but only six arrive, on a clean every-other-month beat — Nov 2025, Jan, Mar, May, Jul, Sep 2026. Either you''re on a bi-monthly tier or half the sends never landed.\n\n**Internal digest (not bulk mail)**\n\n- **Priya Nair — \"[Fernhill Team] Studio weekly\"** — 10 emails, Jan 2025 to Sep 2026. Same digest shape as the others, but it''s your own studio''s weekly, not a subscription. Worth keeping out of any bulk-cleanup.\n\n**Promotional blasts (newsletter-shaped, but one-offs)**\n\n- **Kestrel** — \"15% off this weekend only\" (14 Aug 2026), \"Spring sale starts now\" (20 Mar 2026)\n- **Linkroom** — 4 product announcements: shared recordings (Sep 2026), breakout rooms (Apr 2026), remembered layouts (Sep 2025), live captions in 12 languages (Feb 2025)\n- **Northbeam Air** — 2 route/fare pushes: Osaka from Frankfurt (Jun 2026), \"Summer in Lisbon: city breaks from EUR 79\" (Jun 2025)\n\n**One ghost:** a **Tavola** email dated 7 Mar 2026 reads \"You''re unsubscribed from Tavola picks\" — so a Tavola newsletter existed and you opted out. The newsletter itself isn''t in the mailbox, only the confirmation.\n\n**Two things worth flagging.** First, every one of these stops at **26 September 2026** — Kestrel''s weekly, Codeyard''s weekly, Paperstack''s monthly all go quiet at the same moment, which is the same silence I saw in your bank alerts. That''s a mailbox-wide pattern, not a per-sender one, and it''s the strongest argument yet that something upstream of this inbox stopped delivering around then. Second, none of these carry the `newsletter` label yet, even though the label exists — so your labelling has never been applied to the bulk mail.\n\nWant me to apply `newsletter` to the 67 external ones and `promotional` to the 8 blasts, leaving Priya''s studio weekly alone?","createdAt":1793975344176}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**67 external newsletter/digest emails, from three senders — plus 10 internal digests and 8 promotional blasts.** All of them are read, and all sit in ana@demo.trymetis.email.\n\n**Recurring newsletters and digests**\n\n| Sender | Pattern | Count | Cadence | Latest |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Kestrel Supply Co.** | \"This week at Kestrel: …\" | 56 | weekly | 26 Sep 2026 |\n| **Paperstack** | \"Your Paperstack month: <Month>\" | 6 | every other month | 2 Sep 2026 |\n| **Codeyard** | \"Your weekly Codeyard digest\" | 5 | weekly | 7 Sep 2026 |\n\nKestrel is by far the dominant one — 56 sends going back to Nov 2024, cycling through the same five subjects (\"A kitchen for slow mornings\", \"The candle edit\", \"Stoneware from Porto\", \"Gifts under EUR 30\", \"Notebooks for the new year\", plus \"Meet the maker: Oficina Lume\" and one \"Workshop: kintsugi basics\"). It''s a shop newsletter with a fixed rotation.\n\nPaperstack is the odd one: it calls itself a monthly but only six arrive, on a clean every-other-month beat — Nov 2025, Jan, Mar, May, Jul, Sep 2026. Either you''re on a bi-monthly tier or half the sends never landed.\n\n**Internal digest (not bulk mail)**\n\n- **Priya Nair — \"[Fernhill Team] Studio weekly\"** — 10 emails, Jan 2025 to Sep 2026. Same digest shape as the others, but it''s your own studio''s weekly, not a subscription. Worth keeping out of any bulk-cleanup.\n\n**Promotional blasts (newsletter-shaped, but one-offs)**\n\n- **Kestrel** — \"15% off this weekend only\" (14 Aug 2026), \"Spring sale starts now\" (20 Mar 2026)\n- **Linkroom** — 4 product announcements: shared recordings (Sep 2026), breakout rooms (Apr 2026), remembered layouts (Sep 2025), live captions in 12 languages (Feb 2025)\n- **Northbeam Air** — 2 route/fare pushes: Osaka from Frankfurt (Jun 2026), \"Summer in Lisbon: city breaks from EUR 79\" (Jun 2025)\n\n**One ghost:** a **Tavola** email dated 7 Mar 2026 reads \"You''re unsubscribed from Tavola picks\" — so a Tavola newsletter existed and you opted out. The newsletter itself isn''t in the mailbox, only the confirmation.\n\n**Two things worth flagging.** First, every one of these stops at **26 September 2026** — Kestrel''s weekly, Codeyard''s weekly, Paperstack''s monthly all go quiet at the same moment, which is the same silence I saw in your bank alerts. That''s a mailbox-wide pattern, not a per-sender one, and it''s the strongest argument yet that something upstream of this inbox stopped delivering around then. Second, none of these carry the `newsletter` label yet, even though the label exists — so your labelling has never been applied to the bulk mail.\n\nWant me to apply `newsletter` to the 67 external ones and `promotional` to the 8 blasts, leaving Priya''s studio weekly alone?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-06T14:28:20.601Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
