ible approach: check Offsite 2026 on all 6, and Kaltwasser + Saffron on the full drives (6+6=12) — 18 total. Let me just do Offsite (6), Kaltwasser (7), Saffron (7) = 20 in one batch. I''ll go for it.\n\nHmm, that''s a lot of output. The Offsite folder might have many files. Let''s risk it.\n\nLet me do it.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent — identical names and byte sizes everywhere. So the core content is mirrored across drives.\n\nLet me now verify the remaining bits:\n- Team/Offsite 2026 across 6\n- Clients/Kaltwasser GmbH and Clients/Saffron & Sage on a couple of drives (to confirm they mirror too)\n\nLet me batch Offsite 2026 (6) + Kaltwasser (2: one full drive + the scoped one) + Saffron & Sage (2).\n\nActually let me do Offsite 2026 on all 6, plus welcome.txt read on 2 drives to confirm identical content.\n\nDo I have a readFileText tool? The capabilities mention \"read a plain-text file\". I need to search for it. Let me search \"read file text\".\n\nHmm, but that adds a turn. Let me just do Offsite 2026 on 6 drives and Kaltwasser/Saffron on 2 drives each in this batch, and skip reading file content — sizes matching is strong evidence.\n\nActually reading welcome.txt would confirm content-level identity, strengthening the answer. But sizes + names matching across all levels is already good. The user asked \"do all of those drives have the same files in them?\" — names/inventory comparison is the answer. I''ll note I compared names and sizes, not byte-level contents.\n\nLet me do Offsite 2026 (6) + Kaltwasser GmbH (7) + Saffron & Sage (7) = 20 calls. Too many? Let me do Offsite 2026 (6) + Kaltwasser GmbH on 2 representative drives (sftp full, scoped ftp) + Saffron & Sage on 2 = 10.\n\nHmm, but to claim \"all the same\" I should check the other client folders across all drives. Names matched at the parent level though. Let me be reasonably thorough: Kaltwasser and Saffron on all 7 drives = 14, plus Offsite 2026 on 6 = 20. That''s a lot but let''s do it in one batch — it answers the question definitively.\n\nActually, there''s a risk of hitting too many parallel calls. Let me split: first Offsite 2026 (6) + Kaltwasser GmbH (7) = 13, then Saffron & Sage (7) if needed. Or just do Saffron on 3 representatives.\n\nI think a reasonable, defensible approach: check Offsite 2026 on all 6, and Kaltwasser + Saffron on the full drives (6+6=12) — 18 total. Let me just do Offsite (6), Kaltwasser (7), Saffron (7) = 20 in one batch. I''ll go for it.\n\nHmm, that''s a lot of output. The Offsite folder might have many files. Let''s risk it.\n\nLet me do it."}],"createdAt":1793975425392},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"count":1,"atRoot":false,"entries":[{"fileId":"Team/Offsite 2026/terrace.jpg","name":"terrace.jpg","kind":"file","mimeType":"image/jpeg","size":31270,"modifiedAt":"2026-11-06T14:19:24.000Z","driveId":"36600459-5ed5-55e6-8cb3-f158ce3b8910"}],"cursor":null},"toolCallId":"call_d6dea3e2aeae46aea5d47b97","toolName":"listFolder","args":{"driveId":"36600459-5ed5-55e6-8cb3-f158ce3b8910","folderId":"Team/Offsite 2026/"}},"updatedAt":1793975426056},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"count":1,"atRoot":false,"entries":[{"fileId":"Team/Offsite 2026/terrace.jpg","name":"terrace.jpg","kind":"file","mimeType":"image/jpeg","size":31270,"modifiedAt":null,"driveId":"d4dacf11-803f-51a6-a691-71b4bef60633"}],"cursor":null},"toolCallId":"call_024d850d6ab945c083162139","toolName":"listFolder","args":{"driveId":"d4dacf11-803f-51a6-a691-71b4bef60633","folderId":"Team/Offsite 2026/"}},"updatedAt":1793975426058},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"count":1,"atRoot":false,"entries":[{"fileId":"Team/Offsite 2026/terrace.jpg","name":"terrace.jpg","kind":"file","mimeType":"image/jpeg","size":31270,"modifiedAt":null,"driveId":"42ffd478-fdb0-5b94-a927-24af30e1d0e8"}],"cursor":null},"toolCallId":"call_b5a5715f01b4408299bcd079","toolName"